## SQ-QN-01 | Mending repairs from XP orbs (bot, survival)
@group any
@commands On a scratch server a bot runs it through the `zqn` probe (r1115). `/give @s diamond_pickaxe{Damage:500,Enchantments:[{id:"minecraft:mending",lvl:1}]}`, hold it, `/summon experience_orb ~ ~ ~ {Value:50}`
@pass the pickaxe's damage drops; your XP bar rises less than 50
@fails config not read: check the copied file and Quark's `latest.log` config line
@from batches/r1115/p8_a0.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> pbot spawn qn 105 -60 105 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> xp set qn 0 points
> xp set qn 0 levels
> item replace entity qn weapon.mainhand with minecraft:diamond_pickaxe{Damage:500,Enchantments:[{id:"minecraft:mending",lvl:1}]}
> cdevtest player qn
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=player name=qn .*main="?minecraft:diamond_pickaxe\*1\{Damage:500\b
> summon minecraft:experience_orb 105 -60 105 {Value:50}
> cdevtest tickwarp 60
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=60 30
> cdevtest player qn
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=player name=qn .*xp_total=[0-4]?\d .*main="?minecraft:diamond_pickaxe\*1\{Damage:[0-4]\d\d\b
reject \[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=)
> kill @e[type=minecraft:experience_orb]
look Mending repairs 2 durability per point (50 points = 100 durability): the second `main=` Damage near 400

## SQ-QN-02 | Overworld elytra: the start-fall-flying packet path starts and keeps gliding
@group any
@commands Server half on a bot via `zqn`; the hand feel is a client check (r1115). Overworld: `/give @s elytra`, wear it, `/tp @s ~ ~60 ~`, jump and press jump again while falling
@pass you glide
@fails the dimension lock still applies
@from batches/r1115/p8_a0.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> item replace entity qn armor.chest with minecraft:elytra
> item replace entity qn weapon.mainhand with minecraft:air
> tp qn 105 240 105
sleep 1
> zqn fly qn
waitlog \[zqn\] done 20
expect \[zqn\] fly qn quarkCanUse true onGround false started true fallFlying true chest minecraft:elytra
> cdevtest player qn
> cdevtest tickwarp 40
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=40 30
> cdevtest player qn
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=player name=qn dim=minecraft:overworld .*fall_flying=true
reject \[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=)
> pbot remove qn
look gliding (fall_flying=true in both `verb=player` lines, the second 40 ticks after the start, y lower); the client-side hand check (jump in air) is CQ-style and not run here
